  "bound_exact_form": "For a test h with per-class errors e0=P1[h=1] and e1=P2[h=0], TV(P1,P2) >= 1-e0-e1. For every q in Q, compute one-sided Clopper-Pearson upper limits U0,U1 at alpha/(2|Q|), use the test witness 1-U0-U1 = 1-2*optimistic_error, and take the maximum over q. The returned value is max(0, raw_bound); raw_bound and vacuity are retained in diagnostics.",
  "bound_source": "Michel, Naf, and Meinshausen, High Probability Lower Bounds for the Total Variation Distance, arXiv:2005.06006, population classifier inequality TV(P,Q) >= sup_t[A0(t)+A1(t)]-1. Primary source: https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.06006. The finite-sample Clopper-Pearson/q-ladder construction here is an explicitly labeled own construction, not an attribution to Michel et al. A named primary source for the requested Cohn-Tesoriero form was not recovered.",
